  "result": "Units mismatch. `token.exp` = seconds since epoch (~1.7 \u00d7 10\u2079). `Date.now()` = milliseconds (~1.7 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2).\n\nYour check is probably:\n\n```js\nif (token.exp > Date.now()) { /* reject */ }\n```\n\n`token.exp` (1,745,000,000) always less than `Date.now()` (1,745,000,000,000) \u2192 condition never true \u2192 all tokens pass.\n\nFix \u2014 two options:\n\n```js\n// Option A: convert exp to ms\nif (token.exp * 1000 < Date.now()) {\n  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });\n}\n\n// Option B: convert Date.now() to seconds\nif (token.exp < Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000)) {\n  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });\n}\n```\n\nOption B matches JWT spec (RFC 7519 \u00a74.1.4 uses seconds). Prefer it.",
